Revision history for PDL-IO-NYHead

0.04  2026-10-25
    - PDL::IO::NYHead::Interp: leadfield rows at any point from the electrode rows
      (3-D polyharmonic RBF, phi = r or r^3, with a linear term): interp_weights,
      interp_rows, row_errors, loo (closed form of Rippa 1999 with all electrodes,
      extended to leaving out the electrodes within gap => G mm), distances.
    - PDL::IO::NYHead: interp_rows($pts, kernel =>, k =>, exclude => [names]).
    - examples/nyhead_interp_rows.pl: rows at own points, leave-one-out errors (with a
      gap equal to each point's spacing for the expected error of its row),
      differences of rows for pairs of electrodes and points with their errors.
    - examples/nyhead_neck_electrodes.pl: --along (skin distances along the back
      midline profile).
    - MANIFEST: examples/nyhead_points_usda.pl and the new files.
    - t/05_interp.t, t/06_interp_mat.t.

0.03  2026-10-24
    - PDL::IO::NYHead::H5Dump: read_cell_strings falls back to the low-level
      functions of PDL::IO::HDF5 (H5Dread of H5T_STD_REF_OBJ, H5Rdereference,
      uint16 read) when h5dump is not found. new(method => 'auto'|'h5dump'|
      'lowlevel'), method(), have_h5dump(), read_cell_strings_lowlevel().
    - PDL::IO::NYHead: new($file, strings => ...) and strings_method().
    - examples/check_nyhead.pl: --strings.
    - examples/nyhead_electrodes_3d.pl (moved from PDL-EEG).
    - examples/nyhead_neck_electrodes.pl: neck electrodes against the head mesh and the
      leadfield rows and the RMS of differences of rows (bipolar neck leads); nearest
      NYHead electrode to given points; --arc places points at lengths along the back
      midline of the head mesh from Iz, cut at the cap of the mesh and extended.
    - t/04_lowlevel.t.

0.02  2026-07-23
    - Initial standalone release, split out of the PDL-EEG project.
    - PDL::IO::NYHead: OO reader for the New York Head (sa_nyhead.mat,
      MATLAB v7.3/HDF5). Electrodes (labels + positions), leadfield
      (V_fem / V_fem_normal), head and cortex surfaces, low-resolution
      cortex reconstruction via in_from_cortex75K (PDL fancy index),
      Harvard-Oxford atlas, coordinate transforms, nearest-vertex.
    - Mesh export: to_obj / to_usda / write_mesh (thin wrappers over
      surface()/cortex()). OBJ keeps 1-based faces; USDA emits 0-based
      faceVertexIndices. examples/nyhead_export.pl with --format obj|usda.
    - PDL::IO::NYHead::H5Dump: reads MATLAB v7.3 cell-of-string fields
      (electrode / atlas names) that PDL::IO::HDF5 leaves as unresolved
      object references, via the h5dump CLI. Version-independent #refs#
      delimiter (no dependence on the h5dump object-id output format).
    - Bundled synthetic MATLAB v7.3 fixture so the test suite runs
      without the (large) real sa_nyhead.mat.
